 WINGS alone does not establish use of e-IP.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\",\\\"u18\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"No express grandfathering or technical-unavailability exception appears. 'Where practicable' attaches to SFC review and enhancement, not the submission obligation. Optional fee settlement is a separate facility rather than an exception.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"modality\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"'Must' imposes the selected route requirement; 'can also' permits fee settlement. Statements about integration and enhancements describe SFC system activity without independently imposing reporting or payment deadlines.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Launch occurred on 29 July 2024. The original 29 October endpoint is extended to 29 November; compulsory routing starts on 30 November 2024. Applying that date to each submission event is supported, although migration details remain unavailable.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"dependencies\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The referenced 8 July 2024 circular and dependency external-authorities.24ec50 are unavailable. Their contents cannot be presumed. Pairwise diagnostics provide no factual snapshots and expressly report incomparable bindings, so they establish no counterexample or equivalence.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u3\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Does footnote 1 exhaustively define the product scope or describe IPD's remit without independently limiting the operative wording?\\\",\\n    \\\"Does the unavailable 8 July 2024 circular define qualifying submissions, actor responsibilities or migration arrangements for existing cases?\\\",\\n    \\\"Can the reported incomparable node pairs be supplied with aligned fact definitions and concrete snapshots before treating them as counterexamples?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"readings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\n        \\\"The assessment concerns one identified submission event and only its route.\\\",\\n        \\\"Footnote 1 is an exhaustive product boundary for this circular.\\\",\\n        \\\"Extending the parallel run carries forward existing-channel acceptance through 29 November 2024.\\\",\\n        \\\"The event date controls commencement; no unstated grandfathering exception is assumed.\\\",\\n        \\\"Product administration, product classification and submission classification remain supplied facts; no truth values are inferred.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\":[\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u1\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"new product applications and post-authorisation/registration submissions to IPD.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u3\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u4\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u7\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"}\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"Treats the attached, unqualified product enumeration as an exhaustive definition. Unlike r2, an otherwise qualifying submission concerning an IPD-administered product outside every listed class falls outside this selected control. The strongest uncertainty is that the footnote contains no express exclusivity language. This difference is conditional; the packet establishes no actual unlisted IPD-administered product.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"definitions\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":{\\n        \\\"facts\\\":[\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed event is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product; fee settlement alone is excluded. Classification of borderline communications requires judgment.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"is_product_submission\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The investment product concerned is administered by IPD.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"product_administered_by_ipd\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The investment product concerned belongs to at least one product class enumerated in footnote 1.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"product_in_footnote_classes\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u17\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"Gregorian calendar date on which the assessed application or submission is made to IPD.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"submission_date\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":false,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"date\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Gregorian calendar date\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed application or submission is submitted to IPD via e-IP.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"submitted_via_eip\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":false,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"result\\\":\\\"submitted_via_eip\\\",\\n        \\\"result_type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n        \\\"scope\\\":\\\"(and is_product_submission product_administered_by_ipd product_in_footnote_classes (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"local_id\\\":\\\"r1\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\":[\\n        \\\"Is the footnote intended to exclude any IPD-administered product outside its enumerated classes?\\\",\\n        \\\"Which communications during an existing application count as submissions?\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"statement\\\":\\\"For an application or submission to IPD concerning an IPD-administered product within footnote 1's listed classes, the submitting actor must use e-IP from 30 November 2024. Existing channels remain accepted through the extended parallel run. Annual-fee settlement through e-IP is optional. A true result within scope satisfies only the selected submission-route control; outside scope no compliance determination is made.\\\",\\n      \\\"subject\\\":\\\"Selected control: compulsory e-IP route with an exhaustive footnote product boundary\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\n        \\\"The assessment concerns one identified submission event and only its route.\\\",\\n        \\\"The operative criterion is IPD administration; footnote 1 describes that remit without adding an independent exclusion.\\\",\\n        \\\"Extending the parallel run carries forward existing-channel acceptance through 29 November 2024.\\\",\\n        \\\"The event date controls commencement; no unstated grandfathering exception is assumed.\\\",\\n        \\\"Product administration, product classification and submission classification remain supplied facts; no truth values are inferred.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\":[\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"the SFC launched e-IP on its WINGS2 portal on 29 July 2024\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u3\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"2 Web-based INteGrated Service.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u18\\\"}\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"Gives controlling effect to the repeated functional phrase 'administered by IPD'; footnote membership is descriptive rather than an additional condition. It differs from r1 only if IPD administers a product outside the listed classes. The strongest uncertainty is whether the footnote was intended as a complete definition. Hypotheses restricting the duty to existing e-IP users or conditioning commencement on practicable enhancements fail: the user reference concerns optional fees, and practicability concerns SFC enhancements. The supplied incomparable-pair diagnostics do not resolve any of these questions.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":{\\n        \\\"facts\\\":[\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed event is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product; fee settlement alone is excluded. Classification of borderline communications requires judgment.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"is_product_submission\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The investment product concerned is administered by IPD.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"product_administered_by_ipd\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The investment product concerned belongs to at least one product class enumerated in footnote 1.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"product_in_footnote_classes\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u17\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"Gregorian calendar date on which the assessed application or submission is made to IPD.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"submission_date\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":false,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"date\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Gregorian calendar date\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed application or submission is submitted to IPD via e-IP.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"submitted_via_eip\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":false,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"result\\\":\\\"submitted_via_eip\\\",\\n        \\\"result_type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n        \\\"scope\\\":\\\"(and is_product_submission product_administered_by_ipd (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"local_id\\\":\\\"r2\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\":[\\n        \\\"Can IPD administration extend beyond the footnote classes for purposes of this circular?\\\",\\n        \\\"Does unavailable migration guidance qualify routing for subsequent submissions in existing cases?\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"statement\\\":\\\"From 30 November 2024, an actor making an application or submission to IPD concerning any investment product administered by IPD must use e-IP. Footnote 1 describes the relevant product remit without imposing a separate list-membership condition. Integrated reporting requests illustrate covered submission functions but do not establish reporting deadlines. Fee settlement remains optional, and enhancement practicability does not qualify the route requirement. A true result within scope satisfies only this selected route control.\\\",\\n      \\\"subject\\\":\\\"Selected control: compulsory e-IP route determined by IPD administration\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":27609,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":3016,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":61}}\n","fresh_context":true,"independence":"CONTEXT_ONLY_SAME_MODEL_CORRELATION_UNMEASURED","model":"gpt-6-astra","provider":"codex.fresh.v1","provider_route_hash":"3d676052ff208f9c0b35467659af41d3138476127d0d1b523970689c2edf4714","request_hash":"abbc83460a955503a167b0ff89abb1015d079d4adee2199d6c8fb594d277cf8f","response_hash":"b87a31990c6717284376f72213d20713aab9742bd8bb9c72324a1f4510529925","transport_retry_policy":"NO_APPLICATION_RETRY; CLI transport behavior is external","usage":[{"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0,"input_tokens":27609,"output_tokens":3016,"reasoning_output_tokens":61}],"wall_milliseconds":108747},"response":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Ope